# Design System — Neon Blueprint

ArroBuild uses **Neon Blueprint** (amber + sky on navy), not the retired v2 lime/charcoal look.

## Do

- Accents: `var(--app-amber)` / `var(--app-sky)` (or `--lp-*` on marketing landing)
- Surfaces: `var(--app-bg-base|surface|elevated|hover)`
- Text: `var(--app-text-primary|secondary|tertiary)`
- Primary buttons: `btn btn-primary` (resolves to amber)
- Mini tools pages: wrap with `className="tools-app"` so tokens remap correctly
- Prefer Unbounded + JetBrains Mono like README / Copy Studio / Portfolio

## Don't

- Do **not** use neon lime `#CCFF00` / `#AADA00` or invent new lime tokens
- Do **not** treat `--color-lime` as “bright green” — it is a **legacy alias of amber** only
- Prefer `--app-amber` / `--app-sky` in new code instead of `--color-lime`
- Avoid charcoal flat backgrounds (`#1A1A1A` stacks) on new app pages — use blueprint navy (`#0D1321` / `--app-bg-*`)
- Avoid emoji decoration and rounded-full step pills on tool wizards

## New page checklist

1. Use `AppShell` + blueprint hero pattern from `/tools/readme-generator` or `/tools/copy-studio`
2. Add `tools-app` (mini tools) or `generate-app` / `dashboard-app` / `learn-app` as appropriate
3. Step indicators: equal flex steps, sky progress, hide on result
4. Spot-check: no element should render neon green
